# Godot's import cache and per-machine editor state. Regenerated on open.
.godot/
.import/

# Export output, film frames and check logs - everything a tool writes in here.
#
# `build/*` and not `build/`: a bare `build/` stops git descending into the
# directory at all, so `!build/.gdignore` can never match; adding `!build/`
# to get around that un-ignores the whole DIRECTORY and git then tracks
# everything inside it. Ignoring the CONTENTS and re-including one file is the
# pattern that actually works.
build/*
# ...except the marker that stops Godot importing and EXPORTING what films and
# exports leave in there. Without it the .gdignore is missing on every fresh
# clone, the first editor open imports thousands of film frames, and the
# exporter packs them into the APK.
!build/.gdignore
*.apk
*.aab
*.idsig

# Never commit signing material. The debug keystore is universally known and
# still does not belong here; the release keystore would be a real key leak.
# Keys live in C:\dev\keys, outside every repository.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12

# Godot's Android Gradle build, generated by --install-android-build-template.
# It is the export template unpacked, not source: regenerated on demand, and
# several hundred files of engine code that would drown every diff.
android/


# Redirected run logs. Every hang investigation leaves a few behind.
*.log
timing.txt
probe.txt
